# Code owners for the CI gate: the workflows and the attestation check (.github/), the
# lanes and scripts they call (etc/), the Makefile targets that drive them, `make attest`
# among them, and the tool configuration that decides what the lanes' commands do. The
# `main` ruleset has require_code_owner_review on, so a PR that changes any path below
# needs an approving review from one of the owners listed on it. This file is under
# /.github/, so the same holds for a change to it.
#
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the pull request's base branch, never from the PR itself,
# so a PR cannot change who has to review it. An edit here takes effect once it is on
# main.
#
# Keep the owners in step with MAINTAINERS in the `ci-scope` job of
# .github/workflows/pr.yaml. That list is lowercase; GitHub logins are case-insensitive.
#
# Paths not listed here need the ruleset's approval, but not a code owner's. There is
# deliberately no `*` line: it would change review policy for the whole repository.
#
# The tool configuration changes a lane without touching etc/ci-lanes.sh. `[profile.ci]`
# in .config/nextest.toml is read only by the CI lanes (NEXTEST_PROFILE: ci in pr.yaml),
# never by `make attest`; an alias in .cargo/ can stand in for `cargo nextest`, `cargo
# clippy` or `cargo fmt` in both. Directories and `rust-toolchain*` are matched whole
# because cargo prefers .cargo/config and rustup a bare rust-toolchain over the .toml
# files; rustfmt and clippy read the nearest config above each crate, so those match at
# any depth. The root Cargo.toml stays out: every dependency bump would need an owner,
# and [workspace.lints] there can do no more than an #![allow] in a crate root.

/.github/          @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/etc/              @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/Makefile          @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/.cargo/           @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/.config/          @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/rust-toolchain*   @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
/rust-nightly      @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
rustfmt.toml       @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
.rustfmt.toml      @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
clippy.toml        @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
.clippy.toml       @grantkee @sstanfield @MavenRain @Huwonk
